> Actually, I'm quite alarmed by this. If we have returns of -1 here, where else do we have those as well?

I just went through all of `providers/implementations/cipher/`, and only found that type of fault in `aes_wrap_cipher()`.  This diff (on current master) fixes it:

``` diff
diff --git a/providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_wrp.c b/providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_wrp.c
index f797db4596..efd40f8dc8 100644
--- a/providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_wrp.c
+++ b/providers/implementations/ciphers/cipher_aes_wrp.c
@@ -212,12 +212,12 @@ static int aes_wrap_cipher(void *vctx,
 
     if (outsize < inl) {
         ERR_raise(ERR_LIB_PROV, PROV_R_OUTPUT_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL);
-        return -1;
+        return 0;
     }
 
     len = aes_wrap_cipher_internal(ctx, out, in, inl);
-    if (len == 0)
-        return -1;
+    if (len <= 0)
+        return 0;
 
     *outl = len;
     return 1;
```
